SUMMARY:Talk With Artist TheArthur Wright
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260621T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260621T150000
UID:3d2db4ded4e4289f7a67b70b412d914f@events.yolocountylibrary.org
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a talk with Bay Area artist\, TheArthur Wright. Wr
 ight's art on display in the Blanchard Room of the Stephens-Davis Library 
 throughout June and July. Wright uses the unique process of bleaching his 
 art to make what he calls golden bleach paintings. His art can be found in
  the UN Building in San Francisco\, in colleges and galleries around the w
 orld\, and was featured in an Oprah Winfrey sponsored art show in Chicago.
  His art can be viewed during the library’s open hours. \n\n\nFor more i
 nformation on TheArthur Wright\, visit his site:  thearthurwright.net
LOCATION:Blanchard Room\, Mary L Stephens Davis Branch Library
URL:https://events.yolocountylibrary.org/event/15322767
X-SOURCE:Yolo Library
END:VEVENT
